Integrated advice: Onboarding is a perfect use case for the People, Process, Tools framework. 
1. People: The first week should be almost entirely focused on people. Schedule 1-on-1s for them with every member of the team. Assign them a 'buddy' who isn't their manager.
2. Process: Give them a clear 30-day plan with Foundational goals. 'Week 1: Complete all HR paperwork and meet the team.' 'Week 2: Shadow Person X and learn Tool Y.' Clarity reduces anxiety.
3. Tools: Ensure all their accounts and hardware are set up before their first day. Nothing makes a new hire feel less valued than not being able to log in.

